cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Certified adaptive examination of blood smears: code, pre-registration and results"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ullah
    given-names: Qudrat
    affiliation: "Faculty of Informatics, University of Debrecen"
  - family-names: Harangi
    given-names: Balázs
    affiliation: "Faculty of Informatics, University of Debrecen"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Afridi-7/certified-adaptive-pbs"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code, pre-registration and stored results for a methodological study of what an adaptive examination of a blood
  smear can guarantee about unexamined material: a reimplemented information-saturation stopping rule, limits for
  certifying the absence of rare evidence and for certifying a blast-proportion threshold, and design-based,
  anytime-valid certification of blast-count decisions. Not a clinical tool.
keywords:
  - anytime-valid inference
  - risk-limiting audits
  - adaptive sampling
  - blast count
  - blood smear
